{"header":{"type":"esummary","version":"0.3"},"result":{"uids":["200093871"],"200093871":{"uid":"200093871","accession":"GSE93871","gds":"","title":"Chromatin remodelers CHD9 and BRM are required for dex-regulated expression of block genes in U2OS-GR⍺ cells","summary":"The glucocorticoid-activated glucocorticoid receptor (GR) regulates cellular stress pathways by binding to genomic regulatory elements of target genes and recruiting coregulator proteins to remodel chromatin and regulate transcription complex assembly. The coregulator Hydrogen peroxide-inducible clone 5 (Hic-5) is required for glucocorticoid regulation of some genes, but not others, and blocks regulation of a third gene set. Hic-5 inhibits GR binding to blocked genes but not other glucocorticoid-regulated genes. Site-specific blocking of GR binding is due to gene-specific requirements for ATP-dependent chromatin remodeling enzymes. We investigate whether ATPases CHD9 and BRM were required for glucocorticoid-regulated expression of Hic-5 blocked genes.","gpl":"18573","gse":"93871","taxon":"Homo sapiens","entrytype":"GSE","gdstype":"Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing","ptechtype":"","valtype":"","ssinfo":"","subsetinfo":"","pdat":"2017/06/12","suppfile":"CSV","samples":[{"accession":"GSM2464334","title":"siBRMsiHic5 dex replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM2464354","title":"siCHD9siHic5 dex replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM2464351","title":"siCHD9siNS etoh replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM2464331","title":"siBRMsiNS etoh replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM2464337","title":"siHic5siNS etoh replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM2464343","title":"siBRMsiNS etoh replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM2464323","title":"siNSsiNS etoh replicate 1"},{"accession":"GSM2464357","title":"siBRMsiHic5 etoh replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM2464340","title":"siCHD9siNS dex replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM2464356","title":"siBRMsiNS dex replicate 3"},{"accession":"GSM2464336","title":"siNSsiNS dex replicate 2"},{"accession":"GSM2464345